---
import { GITHUB_URL } from "../config";
const faqs = [
  { q: "Why pay if it's open source?", a: "You're paying for convenience and to keep the project going: a signed, notarized macOS app and a signed Windows installer, ready to run. You can always build it yourself from the source for free." },
  { q: "What does the Servers tab stop?", a: "Only your own Node, Bun, Deno, Python, Ruby and PHP dev servers that have nothing connected to their port, have used almost no CPU, and were orphaned by a closed terminal or agent or have run for 6+ hours. Databases, Docker, editors, agents and language servers are never listed. Each one is re-checked, then asked to exit like Ctrl+C. Available on macOS and Linux; Windows is next." },
  { q: "Does it move files to the Trash?", a: "No. Cleanup is permanent, which is what actually frees the space. That's why every removal goes through a review sheet listing exact paths and rebuild steps first." },
  { q: "What will it never touch?", a: "Source code, lockfiles, virtual environments, global caches, SDKs, and generic dist/ or build/ folders without a matching project file. Inaccessible directories are skipped." },
  { q: "How do updates work?", a: "Gigaflush checks GitHub for a newer version at most twice a day and shows a small banner. Paid builds link to your Polar library, where new versions appear for download. Linux builds link to GitHub Releases." },
  { q: "Does Gigaflush collect any data?", a: "No telemetry, no analytics, no account. The update check is a plain request to GitHub's public API. Scanning and cleanup happen entirely on your machine." },
  { q: "How accurate are the sizes?", a: "They're logical file-size estimates. Actual disk savings can differ with filesystem compression, clones, or hard links." },
  { q: "Something isn't working.", a: "Open an issue on GitHub or email support. If it doesn't work on your machine, see the refund terms." },
];
---

<section class="section faq-wrap">
  <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
    <h2>Good to know.</h2>
    <p>Anything else? <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/issues`}>Ask on GitHub</a> or visit <a href="/support">support</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq">
    {
      faqs.map((f, i) => (
        <details name="faq" data-reveal style={`--d:${i % 4}`}>
          <summary>
            {f.q}
            <span class="plus" aria-hidden="true" />
          </summary>
          <p>{f.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq-wrap {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
    gap: 56px;
  }
  .section-head a {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--line-strong);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  .faq {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  details::details-content {
    block-size: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition:
      block-size 500ms var(--ease),
      content-visibility 500ms allow-discrete;
  }
  details[open]::details-content {
    block-size: auto;
  }
  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 22px 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 17px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    transition: color 200ms;
  }
  summary:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .plus {
    position: relative;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--control);
    transition:
      transform 500ms var(--ease),
      background-color 200ms;
  }
  .plus::before,
  .plus::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%;
    top: 50%;
    width: 11px;
    height: 1.6px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--text);
    translate: -50% -50%;
  }
  .plus::after {
    rotate: 90deg;
  }
  details[open] .plus {
    transform: rotate(135deg);
    background: var(--selected);
  }
  details p {
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-bottom: 22px;
    max-width: 40em;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .faq-wrap {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
